# EcoCampus AI — Feature Specification

## 1. Core MVP Features

### Institution Setup
- Register an institution.
- Record institution type, population, buildings, and facilities.
- Add or configure campus zones.
- Upload or manually configure a campus map.
- Review and approve AI-generated setup recommendations.

### Campus Map
- Display campus buildings and zones.
- Mark waste bins and disposal facilities.
- Provide disposal guidance for each waste category.
- Identify reported cleanliness hotspots.

### Student Awareness
- Explain waste segregation.
- Provide environmental awareness content.
- Offer safe, voluntary eco-missions.
- Track verified participation.
- Show collective campus progress.

### Cleanliness Reporting
- Submit a report with category, location, description, and optional photo.
- Track report status.
- Prevent obvious duplicate reports where practical.
- Allow authorised staff to review, assign, and resolve reports.
- Record resolution evidence and status history.

### Administration Dashboard
- View reports and their current status.
- Identify recurring cleanliness hotspots.
- Track issue resolution times.
- Review participation and awareness activity.
- Monitor progress across campus zones.

## 2. AI-Assisted Features
- Help administrators configure institution information.
- Identify missing setup details.
- Suggest potential bin locations for human approval.
- Generate contextual waste-disposal guidance.
- Summarise recurring issues and recommend improvements.

AI-generated recommendations must be clearly labelled and reviewable.

## 3. Future Features
- Support multiple institutions with separate portals.
- Add more advanced campus-map imports.
- Integrate waste sensors where available.
- Improve image-based waste identification.
- Add cross-institution comparisons using privacy-preserving aggregate data.

## 4. Out of Scope for the Initial MVP
- Automatic physical waste sorting hardware.
- Guaranteed waste-generation predictions from population alone.
- Unverified claims about environmental impact.
- Automatic closure of reports without authorised verification.
- Public shaming or punitive student rankings.

## 5. MVP Success Criteria
- An institution can configure its campus.
- Students can access disposal guidance.
- Students can submit and track cleanliness reports.
- Staff can update and verify report resolution.
- Dashboard metrics reflect actual stored records.
- Student participation is tracked transparently.
- Institution data is protected from unauthorised access.
